Vodacom Namecheck

1. Bank to Wallet

Endpoint URL: https://10.11.6.110:8443/api/v1/banktowallet/namecheck

Request:

<mobileNumberInquireReq
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
    <mobileNumber>243999967426</mobileNumber>
    <timestamp>12-Nov-2024 11:13:20</timestamp>
    <msgId>000517665460</msgId>
    <telcom>VODACOM</telcom>
    <channel>OMNI</channel>
    <signature>jZzbRrd8Ycwg8xClrOdddkZcHjXHnUtA6q7CYPPHLFIBVpevEpTNp9WTm80RWYr8oZx5jT8i4FAFMnN58kXd1/QHfjgMxvfkP+T3XmFg2Kv5PdF7rOF0XvsaY9u6hfy2NbnQwaSMg==</signature>
    <bankId>43</bankId>
</mobileNumberInquireReq>

Success Response:

<MobileNumberInquireRes
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
    <msgId>000517665460</msgId>
    <channel>OMNI</channel>
    <telcom>VODACOM</telcom>
    <mobileNumber>243999967426</mobileNumber>
    <responseCode>00</responseCode>
    <customerNames>christian christian christian</customerNames>
</MobileNumberInquireRes>

Failure Response:

<MobileNumberInquireRes
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
    <msgId>000517665460</msgId>
    <channel>OMNI</channel>
    <telcom>VODACOM</telcom>
    <mobileNumber>243999967426</mobileNumber>
    <responseCode>00</responseCode>
    <customerNames>243999967426</customerNames>
</MobileNumberInquireRes>


2. Float Purchase (cashallocation)

Endpoint URL: https://10.11.6.110:8443/api/v1/floatpurchase/namecheck

Request:

<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<mobileNumberInquireReq
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
    <mobileNumber>97093</mobileNumber>
    <tillNumber>97093</tillNumber>
    <timestamp>11-Mar-2025 15:05:09</timestamp>
    <msgId>000610380874</msgId>
    <telcom>VODACOM</telcom>
    <channel>OMNI</channel>
    <bankId>43</bankId>
    <signature>jZzbRrd8YcHfjgMxvfkP+T3XmFg2Kv5PdF7rOF0XvsaY9u6hfy2NbnQwaSMg==</signature>
</mobileNumberInquireReq>

Success Respose:

<MobileNumberInquireRes
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
    <msgId>000610380874</msgId>
    <channel>OMNI</channel>
    <telcom>M-Pesa</telcom>
    <mobileNumber>97093</mobileNumber>
    <responseCode>00</responseCode>
    <customerNames>XYZ Limited</customerNames>
</MobileNumberInquireRes>

Failure Response:

<MobileNumberInquireRes
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
    <msgId>000610380874</msgId>
    <channel>OMNI</channel>
    <telcom>M-Pesa</telcom>
    <mobileNumber>97093</mobileNumber>
    <responseCode>01</responseCode>
    <customerNames></customerNames>
</MobileNumberInquireRes>


Notes:
1. For float purchase namecheck: This is blocking. If responseCode is not 00, then you should not proceed with cashallocation request.
2. For b2w namecheck: This is not blocking, I will always return mobile number as a value in customerNames incase of a namecheck request failure.
3. Omni is using jwt for these post requests


